join Naledi (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Naledi: You manage that roller better than I expected.
- Thank you?
	Hope: Thank you?
	Naledi: It wasn't entirely a compliment. It was an assessment.
	Naledi: Mama Zulu can't make the trip anymore. Ezekiel can, but it costs him the whole morning and his farm needs that morning.
	Naledi: Alternate days. One of them, then the other. Not every day — you'd resent it by the second week and then you'd stop.
	- I wouldn't resent it
		Hope: I wouldn't resent it.
		Naledi: Everyone resents it by the second week. That's why I said alternate days.
		set {GameState.quest_naledi_alternate_rotation_main} = "active"
	- What do they give back?
		Hope: What do they give back?
		Naledi: Good. Ask that.
		Naledi: Mama Zulu knows roots and what they're for. Ezekiel knows why your garden isn't growing. Neither will offer unless you're there often enough to be asked.
		set {GameState.quest_naledi_alternate_rotation_main} = "active"
	[signal arg="objective:Run water to Mama Zulu and Ezekiel on alternate days"]
